\b Visualization behavior right now\b0\par
1. The panel can inspect any selected node with visualizable output.\par
2. Dedicated EEG Visualization nodes are still used for explicit compare workflows.\par
3. Raw vs PSD is inferred automatically from the upstream path; the user no longer manually picks that mode.\par
4. Time-frequency is not implemented yet; the UI has a placeholder state for it.\par
\par
\b Marker behavior right now\b0\par
1. Marker edits in the raw browser are draft-only at first.\par
2. Save Markers commits the change.\par
3. On save, BrainStory auto-creates or reuses an "Add/Remove Markers" node downstream and stores the marker payload there.\par
4. Discard Changes throws the marker draft away.\par
\par
\b Execution / UX behavior right now\b0\par
1. Running nodes from the context menu now shows a top overlay with an indeterminate progress bar.\par
2. This is mainly to make initialization-heavy steps (especially import) feel responsive instead of frozen.\par
3. True background execution is not really implemented yet; this is more of a clear "busy" phase.\par
\par
\b Wire / canvas behavior right now\b0\par
1. Nodes connect by clicking bodies, not tiny circles.\par
2. Downstream must be below or to the right.\par
3. Wires use top/bottom or left/right anchors depending on layout.\par
4. Node cards are fixed-size so wire anchors match their visible boundaries.\par
5. Wires can be selected and deleted.\par
\par
\b Color / visual language right now\b0\par
Category colors currently:\par
- Import = green\par
- Transform = indigo\par
- Markers and Metadata = yellow\par
- Visualize = teal\par
- Export = pink\par
\par
Node states:\par
- yellow-ish border = selected / connection-ready\par
- green outer glow = done\par
